w: How shall I fol- low Him I serve? How shall I co- py Him I love?
w: Pri- va- tions, sor- rows, bit- ter scorn, The life of toil, the mean ab- ode,
w: But when, my days with com- forts crowned As hus- band and as par- ent blessed,
w: Oh, let me think how Thou didst leave Un- tas- ted ev- ery pure de- light,
w: To faint, to grieve, to die for me! Thou cam- est, not Thy- self to please!
w: Yes, I would count them all but loss, To gain the no- tice of Thine eye.
